## Thinking

Ravi needs a used road bike to commute and will pay at most $194. In this sealed-bid double auction, the cleared price is the midpoint of the *last* matched pair. If I bid my true maximum ($194), I maximize my chance of getting matched (since Ravi actually needs the bike), while the midpoint mechanism with the corresponding seller's ask will almost certainly produce a price well below $194. Shading my bid risks failing to match at all, which is worse than paying a slightly higher midpoint. Bidding $194 is the truthful and dominant strategy here.

